{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l17ih7a9","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"physics","chapter":"laws-of-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"newtons-laws-of-motion","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-wire-which-passes-through-the-hole-in-a-small-bead-is-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-zxigphpw0lgqkakl","content":"<p>A wire, which passes through the hole in a small bead, is bent in the form of quarter of a circle. The wire is fixed vertically on ground as shown in the below figure. The bead is released from near the top of the wire and it slides along the wire without friction. As the bead moves from A to B, the force it applies on the wire is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 11 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l17p7vc5/b9f32ced-20af-405f-88c0-f059ac935d39/f0fbc060-aced-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17p7vc6.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"always radially outwards."},{"identifier":"B","content":"always radially inwards."},{"identifier":"C","content":"radially outwards initially and radially inwards later."},{"identifier":"D","content":"radially inwards initially and radially outwards later."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Let v be speed of the bead when it makes an angle <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.061ex\" height=\"1.618ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 469 715\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> with the vertical direction.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 11 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l17pi3x7/e650938b-3633-4d38-9af8-405f375e965f/0db4b2b0-acef-11ec-915c-c385b35e7182/file-1l17pi3x8.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The forces acting on the bead are its weight mg and normal reaction N. Since all the forces acting on the bead are conservative, the mechanical energy of the bead is conserved i.e.,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"23.099ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 10209.8 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(878,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1358,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1809,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2198,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2920.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3920.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"63\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-63\"></use><use data-c=\"6F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6F\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\" transform=\"translate(944,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5258.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5425.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5894.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6560.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7616.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(8410.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(9288.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(518,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ..... (1)</p>\n<p>The radially inward components of force provide centripetal acceleration to the bead i.e.,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"21.93ex\" height=\"2.452ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 9692.9 1083.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(878,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1524.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"63\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-63\"></use><use data-c=\"6F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6F\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\" transform=\"translate(944,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2862.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3029.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3720.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4720.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5886.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6942.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7820.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(518,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8741.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(9241.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ...... (2)</p>\n<p>Eliminate v<sup>2</sup> from equations (1) and (2) to get</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.729ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 8720.3 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1165.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2221.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3099.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3579.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3968.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4635.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"63\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-63\"></use><use data-c=\"6F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6F\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\" transform=\"translate(944,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5973.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6139.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6831.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(7831.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8331.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ...... (3)</p>\n<p>When 3cos<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.061ex\" height=\"1.618ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 469 715\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> &gt; 2, direction of N will be same as shown in figure, i.e., radially outward.</p>\n<p>When 3cos<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.061ex\" height=\"1.618ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 469 715\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> &lt; 2, direction of N will be radially inward. Now, normal on the bead is opposite to the force applied on the wire by the bead, following Newton's third law. Therefore, the force applied on the bead by the wire is radially inwards initially and radially outwards later, as it moves from A to B.</p>"}]}